meta {
  name: preview fleet
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/infra/stacks/kontra-fleet%2Fprobe-bruno/preview
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{stateToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "args": {
      "role": "crawl",
      "machines": 1
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: lte 502
}

docs {
  AUTHENTICATED with the STATE token — deliberately the narrower one. Reading a dataset
  and provisioning cloud machines are not the same privilege, and the explore token is handed
  out for the workbench.

  Starts a `preview` workflow and returns immediately with `{fqn, op, workflowId, runId}`. The
  route NEVER blocks on Pulumi: a ten-machine `up` takes minutes, longer than any proxy holds a
  connection.

  The stack fqn is URL-encoded (`kontra-fleet%2Fprobe-bruno`) because it contains a slash.
  It is also the workflow id — which is what makes two concurrent `up`s on one stack impossible.
}
